  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34674506",
      "title": "Error Handling via ErrorBoundary",
      "lectureOrder": 27,
      "videoOrder": 23,
      "sourceHash": "d9b3adef039617605485443db596def8c9e0d9a0bcf0e5c946eeb2e8d9c558ec",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.19,
          "end": 4.98,
          "en": "At this point, we already made good progress",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.98,
          "end": 9.48,
          "en": "and we're almost done for this essentials section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.48,
          "end": 11.19,
          "en": "However, there are still a couple",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 13.5,
          "en": "of crucial features that are missing, and one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.5,
          "end": 18.06,
          "en": "of them is error handling because things can go wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.06,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "Here for example, in our action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 22.68,
          "en": "the file or the database where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.68,
          "end": 25.8,
          "en": "we're storing data could temporarily be unavailable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.8,
          "end": 28.92,
          "en": "or overwhelmed or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.92,
          "end": 31.35,
          "en": "So saving the data could fail, and of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.35,
          "end": 33.333,
          "en": "reading the data could also fail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 38.22,
          "en": "Now, to simulate this, we could delete this file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.22,
          "end": 40.65,
          "en": "but here I'll not delete it, I'll just rename it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.65,
          "end": 42.63,
          "en": "so that it's not found anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.63,
          "end": 45.48,
          "en": "I deleted the n here at the end of the extension",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.48,
          "end": 48.84,
          "en": "and therefore this file, this notes.jso file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.84,
          "end": 51.423,
          "en": "for which we're looking does not exist anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.59,
          "end": 55.68,
          "en": "Therefore, now if we save this and I reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.68,
          "end": 58.26,
          "en": "I get this ugly error page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.26,
          "end": 62.58,
          "en": "because our server essentially crashed or we got an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.58,
          "end": 66.84,
          "en": "at least, and this default error page is being shown.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 66.84,
          "end": 70.47,
          "en": "Now, typically you don't wanna use that default error page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 70.47,
          "end": 72.69,
          "en": "Instead you wanna show your own error page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 72.69,
          "end": 76.05,
          "en": "and you can easily do that with Remix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.05,
          "end": 78.66,
          "en": "For example, we can go to this root component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.66,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "and in there we can export another new function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 85.98,
          "en": "And that function is called Error boundary like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.98,
          "end": 88.95,
          "en": "And it's actually a component which we're exporting here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.95,
          "end": 91.473,
          "en": "Therefore it starts with an uppercase E.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 92.61,
          "end": 95.64,
          "en": "This is a special function, a special component though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.64,
          "end": 98.7,
          "en": "which must be named like this because just like links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.7,
          "end": 101.91,
          "en": "and action and so on, Remix will be looking for this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.91,
          "end": 102.93,
          "en": "This is a component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.93,
          "end": 104.16,
          "en": "Remix will display",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.16,
          "end": 107.4,
          "en": "if an error occurs anywhere in your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.4,
          "end": 108.84,
          "en": "So on any page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.84,
          "end": 111.47999999999999,
          "en": "since I'm doing this in the root component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.47999999999999,
          "end": 113.49000000000001,
          "en": "I will soon show you how you can add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.49000000000001,
          "end": 115.59,
          "en": "to other pages as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.59,
          "end": 117.74000000000001,
          "en": "But here we'll do it in the root component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.65,
          "end": 123.65,
          "en": "Now, in there, I now wanna return my HTML skeleton",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.96,
          "end": 127.53,
          "en": "so I'll grab that, but I'll adjust it a little bit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 127.53,
          "end": 130.44,
          "en": "For example, I'll add a title here, which we can do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.44,
          "end": 134.61,
          "en": "We can add any default HTML elements here in this skeleton.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 134.61,
          "end": 139.61,
          "en": "And here I'll add a title to head and say an error occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.51,
          "end": 145.29,
          "en": "And then here I still output my main navigation maybe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 145.29,
          "end": 147.06,
          "en": "but instead of the outlet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.06,
          "end": 152.06,
          "en": "I'll output a main section here where I have a H1 element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.25,
          "end": 155.28300000000002,
          "en": "with a text of an error occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 159.963,
          "en": "And then below that, maybe the error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 160.89,
          "end": 164.49,
          "en": "Now this special component always gets an error prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 164.49,
          "end": 165.54,
          "en": "which we can get hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 165.54,
          "end": 168.69,
          "en": "of with object destructuring like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.69,
          "end": 171.87,
          "en": "And this prop will be provided or a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.87,
          "end": 174.78,
          "en": "for this prop will be provided by Remix because",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 174.78,
          "end": 178.473,
          "en": "Remix will create this component when an error occurs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 179.4,
          "end": 182.43,
          "en": "This is the default JavaScript error object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 182.43,
          "end": 186.24,
          "en": "So the value here on this error prop is an object based",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.24,
          "end": 190.08,
          "en": "on this default JavaScript error object constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 190.08,
          "end": 192.39,
          "en": "And therefore we'll have a message property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 192.39,
          "end": 193.653,
          "en": "which we can access here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 195.15,
          "end": 197.64,
          "en": "We could then also add some extra text",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.64,
          "end": 201.27,
          "en": "which maybe says back to safety.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 201.27,
          "end": 205.53,
          "en": "And safety should maybe be wrapped by the link component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 205.53,
          "end": 208.74,
          "en": "So this default Remix link component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 208.74,
          "end": 213.453,
          "en": "which therefore also must be imported from Remix run React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.4,
          "end": 218.223,
          "en": "And here I simply want to go back to the starting page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.95,
          "end": 223.65,
          "en": "With that if we save this and we reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.65,
          "end": 225.66,
          "en": "I get my own error page here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 225.66,
          "end": 228.18,
          "en": "As you can tell, now the styling is a bit off",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.18,
          "end": 231.57,
          "en": "but it can be fixed by adding a special class to main here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 231.57,
          "end": 234.96,
          "en": "the error class for which I define some styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 237.753,
          "en": "in one of the style files I provided earlier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.77,
          "end": 242.19,
          "en": "With that, I got this error look here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 244.53,
          "en": "and it can of course go back to safety",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 244.53,
          "end": 247.8,
          "en": "but whenever I go back to notes, it crashes again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.8,
          "end": 250.23,
          "en": "So that's how you can add your own error page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.23,
          "end": 254.85,
          "en": "your own error component with help of this error boundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 254.85,
          "end": 256.68,
          "en": "However, you are not limited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.68,
          "end": 259.29,
          "en": "to just adding this to the root component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 259.29,
          "end": 260.79,
          "en": "Instead you can add this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 260.79,
          "end": 265.68,
          "en": "this special error boundary component in any Route file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 265.68,
          "end": 267.78,
          "en": "If you only have it in the root component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 267.78,
          "end": 271.29,
          "en": "this will simply handle all errors that occur anywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 271.29,
          "end": 275.403,
          "en": "So it's the last resort of error catching, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 276.36,
          "end": 277.193,
          "en": "But if we know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.193,
          "end": 279.75,
          "en": "that things could go wrong on our notes Route here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 279.75,
          "end": 284.19,
          "en": "it might make sense to add a separate error boundary here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 284.19,
          "end": 286.89,
          "en": "And then here we could return some content that's tailored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 286.89,
          "end": 289.44,
          "en": "for this specific page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 289.44,
          "end": 291.69,
          "en": "And actually what's then important to keep in mind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 291.69,
          "end": 296.07,
          "en": "and to understand is that if you have an error boundary",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 296.07,
          "end": 298.83,
          "en": "on a Route that's not the root Route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 298.83,
          "end": 302.34,
          "en": "only the content of that Route which failed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 302.34,
          "end": 305.25,
          "en": "will be replaced by the error boundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 305.25,
          "end": 309.21,
          "en": "So only this page content will be replaced.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.21,
          "end": 312.6,
          "en": "So if I have an error boundary here in notes jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.6,
          "end": 316.71,
          "en": "this content returned by this error boundary component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 316.71,
          "end": 320.4,
          "en": "will be injected in my default skeleton here in place",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 320.4,
          "end": 321.273,
          "en": "of the outlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 322.47,
          "end": 326.91,
          "en": "So therefore, now with that, I could copy this part here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 326.91,
          "end": 331.91,
          "en": "and just this part of my root error outlet and add it here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 331.95,
          "end": 335.223,
          "en": "and return it as part of this error boundary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 336.48,
          "end": 339,
          "en": "We now just need to make sure that we again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 339,
          "end": 342.153,
          "en": "use this error prop, which we're getting automatically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 343.77,
          "end": 348.77,
          "en": "I now also must import link here from Remix run React again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 350.67,
          "end": 354.24,
          "en": "And with that added, we get the same output as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 354.24,
          "end": 357.24,
          "en": "but technically what happens under the hood",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 357.24,
          "end": 359.07,
          "en": "is different now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 359.07,
          "end": 362.91,
          "en": "because now we're actually using this error boundary",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 362.91,
          "end": 365.37,
          "en": "and therefore we could also tailor this more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 365.37,
          "end": 367.26,
          "en": "for this specific scenario.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 367.26,
          "end": 369.78,
          "en": "And for example, replace an error occurred",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 369.78,
          "end": 372.66,
          "en": "with an error related",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 372.66,
          "end": 377.433,
          "en": "to your notes occurred, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 378.3,
          "end": 381.63,
          "en": "And now you will see that this error boundary is being used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 381.63,
          "end": 383.883,
          "en": "because you see this message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 387.27,
          "en": "So that's how you can handle errors",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 387.27,
          "end": 389.85,
          "en": "and how easy it is to handle errors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 389.85,
          "end": 391.65,
          "en": "You don't have to manage any error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 391.65,
          "end": 394.53,
          "en": "or state in your component and check",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 394.53,
          "end": 396.81,
          "en": "if there is an error or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 396.81,
          "end": 399.96,
          "en": "You simply define this fallback component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 399.96,
          "end": 402.36,
          "en": "and it will automatically be rendered whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 402.36,
          "end": 404.85,
          "en": "an error occurs in this Route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 404.85,
          "end": 408.3,
          "en": "or in case of the root component here, the root Route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 408.3,
          "end": 410.103,
          "en": "anywhere in the application.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
